    "frames": [
      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "source": "carousel-art-director",
        "subject": "A teal tracked triage rover drawn close and large on pale broken concrete. Its mast head sends a cyan scan cone out to the left, and a lime arc from its radio box lands on the rugged tablet held by a medic in blue coveralls, seen from behind against stacked slabs with a red first-aid bag.",
        "visual_consequence": "With no words, the machine senses and the person receives. The single lime arc is the only accent line in the frame and runs from the rover's radio into the tablet in the medic's hands. At 432 px the rover, the arc and the standing medic read as separate shapes, and the headline sits in clean sky above the mast.",
        "weakness": "The foreground casualty's boot soles at lower left read at native size as smooth brown capsules, a kit mannequin part. The scan cone ends on the yellow building fragment rather than the casualty. The mast head is a stack of black boxes, and the bottom fifth is soft smeared concrete.",
        "repair": "Take the casualty's boots out of frame or hide them behind a rubble slab, then aim the scan cone down toward that off-frame point at the left edge.",
        "encoding_reads": true,
        "dominant_subject_finished": true,
        "feed_legible": true,
